  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1248 AM MST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nQuiet weather is forecast across central and northern NM mid-week \nthrough the weekend. A ridge will amplify over the Intermountain \nWest Tuesday into Wednesday, moderating temperatures and keeping \nwinds light. High clouds begin to increase from the west on \nThanksgiving Day. Dry northwest flow will continue through Saturday \nas a trough deepens over Mexico to the south. This will create a \nnorthwest breeze for the typical windy spots just east of the \ncentral mountain chain while most areas maintain light winds.\n\nAs has been advertised, the pattern looks to become more active \nduring the first week of December due to the intensification of the \njet stream over the eastern Pacific. This will favor a more active \nstorm track and increase the likelihood that a storm system moves \ninto the desert southwest. Given the influence of the sub-tropical \njet, warmer temperatures would be favored so seasonably high snow \nlevels would occur with any approaching storm system early next \nweek.",
